cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  switch-pipeline: de novo design of a single sequence compatible
  with two target-bound conformations
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vassen
    given-names: Maximilian
repository-code: https://github.com/Maximilianvsn/switch-pipeline
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A design pipeline that generates a state-1 binder backbone with
  RFdiffusion3, derives a second state by partial diffusion, and designs one
  sequence tied across both states with DynamicMPNN (with ProteinMPNN-MSD as
  an equal-budget comparator). Candidates are selected by an AlphaFold2
  initial-guess two-state gate calibrated against paired,
  composition-matched scramble nulls, then scored with Boltz-2. All reported
  metrics are predictor confidence, not affinity or free energy.
keywords:
  - protein design
  - de novo binder design
  - multi-state design
  - RFdiffusion
  - AlphaFold2
  - null calibration
